 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The wind is born again.\nA carpet of white snows, like flowers,\nWhispers in the nightingales' voices\nWhere the endless mountain,\nWhere the forest tapers low,\nCries through its vastening thinnest boughs.\nBlue skies against that blue sky shadows\nBlows dappled mists to sleep. Again,\nFresh from the deluge again,\nSea and fire again,\nCame a flood away for me; again\nI flitted on through forests dark",
